# Design tokens — required

Single source of truth:

`src/styles/design-tokens.css`

Guide: `docs/DESIGN.md`.

## Do

- Use semantic Tailwind classes (`bg-primary`, `text-foreground`, `font-serif`,
  `bg-warning`, …) or CSS vars like `var(--color-primary)`, `var(--font-body)`.
- Token names are **generic**: `primary`, `secondary`, `accent`, `muted`,
  `destructive`, `warning`, `background`, `foreground` — not brand nicknames.
- If something is missing, add a generic token in the design file first.

## Don't

- Hardcode `lab()`, `oklch()`, `#hex`, `rgb()`, `hsl()` in feature components.
- Invent brand nicknames for tokens.
- Rebrand by editing scattered component styles — only edit `design-tokens.css`
  (and hex mirrors in `src/lib/design-tokens.ts` + favicon assets).

## Exceptions

- Third-party brand colors (Google logo SVG).
- Static favicon/apple-icon assets (hex mirrors must match the carta).
